Kit 1.1.0 is usable (2026-11-15; verified on a real render: -20.0 LUFS, true peak -6.1 dBTP, fades pass). What changed (full list and the film migration checklist: video/kit/CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0; rules: video/README.md; catalog: video/kit/README.md): demo films are text-first with NO voice of any kind and one instrumental music bed; the next-steps block leaves the template and films (QA fails a `nextsteps` host); the end card stays <= 3 s with name and haiderb.com (closing question optional: "question": "" gives the sign-off alone); the palette follows the demo UI revamp (ground #0a0a0f, ink #f2f1f9) with ONE accent per film set on the root as data-kit-accent="iris" (Distru) | "cobalt" (AssemblyAI) | "coral" (Great Question). Adopt it with `node kit/scripts/sync.mjs <slug>` from /home/claude/demos-all/video (sync only your own film). Music: put `<!-- kit:music:start -->` and `<!-- kit:music:end -->` inside the root div of index.html after the scene hosts, then run `node kit/scripts/music-bed.mjs films/<slug> [--bed bright-pluck-112] [--align end|start]` once the film's length is final (re-run after any length change): it writes one `<audio id="music" class="clip kit-music" src="assets/music/<bed>.mp3" data-start="0" data-duration="<film>" data-media-start=... data-volume=<measured for -20 LUFS> data-fade-in="0.3" data-fade-out="1.5" ...>` (by default the bed's own ending lands on the last frame) and vendors the mp3 into assets/music/ (sync does too; git-ignored). Captions v2 (compositions/captions.html; skeleton in kit/components/caption-band.html): band `<div id="cap-band" class="clip" data-start="0" data-duration="D" data-layout-ignore><div class="kit-band kit-band2"></div></div>`, stepper `<div id="cap-progress" class="clip kit-progress" data-start="0" data-duration="D" data-kit-steps="Email,Extract,Check,..." data-layout-ignore></div>`, and one cue at a time `<div id="cap-x" class="clip kit-cap kit-cap2" data-start data-duration data-kit-step="2"><div class="kit-cap-kicker"><span>Step 2 · Check</span>[<span class="kit-speed" data-rate="6" data-tag-start data-tag-end>6x</span>|<span class="kit-chip">Cached replay</span>]</div><div class="kit-cap-head">One headline, <= ~10 words, *accent* word</div><div class="kit-cap-detail">Optional detail, <= ~14 words.</div></div>` (headline 58 px on one line, detail 32 px on one line; Kit.captions.animate unchanged). Annotation (in a footage scene, outside .kit-stage; kit/components/annotation.html): `<div id="s-ann-x" class="clip kit-ann" data-start data-duration data-kit-focus="<tracked component>" [data-kit-side="auto|right|left|below|above"] data-track-index="3" data-layout-allow-overlap data-layout-allow-occlusion><div class="kit-ann-label">Label of 6 words or fewer</div></div>`; Kit.scene.footage places ring + label automatically inside the safe area, never over the shot's focus box, the ring or the band (preferring whitespace; a leader line when it sits outside the focus box); give the focus room with a lower maxZoom. QA (`node kit/scripts/qa.mjs films/<slug> [--frames] [--video renders/x.mp4]`) now FAILS on: no music bed or more than one; any other <audio>, <video data-has-audio> or un-muted video with sound (unless data-kit-audio-reason="..."); a bed that does not run 0 to the film's end with fade-in <= 0.3 s, a fade-out and a level; a next-steps host; two captions or two annotations on screen at once; any cue, annotation or cold-open headline on screen less than 0.6 s + 0.35 s per word (head + detail + chips; kicker and speed tags not counted, so a 2.2 s cold open carries <= 4 headline words); a v2 headline or detail that does not fit one line, a headline over 12 words (WARN 11-12), detail over 16 (WARN 15-16), headline under 52 px; annotations over 6 words, outside one camera hold, ring outside the safe area or with no label placement; with --video: integrated loudness outside -22..-18 LUFS, true peak above -1 dBTP, no fade-in/fade-out, not H.264 1920x1080 30 fps + audio, or >= 20 MB. It WARNS on v1 cues and a missing data-kit-accent; the "silent" expectation is retired and the framing sheet now shows each annotation. From here on kit changes are additive and logged in CHANGELOG.md.
